---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const rules = (await getCollection('rules')).sort((a, b) => a.data.rule - b.data.rule);

// Countdown is computed at build time. Rebuild (or redeploy) refreshes it.
const TARGET = new Date('2027-05-13T00:00:00+05:30');
const now = new Date();
const daysLeft = Math.ceil((TARGET.getTime() - now.getTime()) / 86_400_000);

const stages = [
  {
    date: '13 November 2025',
    act: 'ss. 2, 18–26, 35–43, 44(1),(3)',
    rules: '1, 2, 17–21',
    what: 'Building the regulator',
    cls: 'pill-now',
    status: 'In force',
  },
  {
    date: '13 November 2026',
    act: 's.6(9), s.27(1)(d)',
    rules: '4',
    what: 'Consent Manager registration',
    cls: 'pill-soon',
    status: 'Next',
  },
  {
    date: '13 May 2027',
    act: 'ss. 3–5, 6(1)–(8),(10), 7–17, 27–34, 36, 37',
    rules: '3, 5–16, 22, 23',
    what: 'Everything that burdens business',
    cls: 'pill-later',
    status: 'The deadline',
  },
];
---

<Base title="DPDP Rules 2025 — rule by rule" wide>
  <h1>The DPDP Rules, 2025</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every Rule and Schedule of the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025, read together
    with the duty in the Act it serves — and the clause of section 40(2) that authorised it.
  </p>

  <div class="countdown">
    <div class="days">{daysLeft}</div>
    <div class="cap">days until 13 May 2027, when the obligations on business commence</div>
  </div>

  <h2>The law commences in three stages</h2>
  <p>
    Both the Act and the Rules were switched on by two notifications issued the same day —
    G.S.R. 843(E) for the Act, G.S.R. 846(E) for the Rules. They are deliberately in lockstep.
  </p>

  <div class="scroll-x">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Date</th><th>Act sections</th><th>Rules</th><th>What it is</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {stages.map((s) => (
          <tr>
            <td>
              <strong>{s.date}</strong><br />
              <span class:list={['pill', s.cls]}>{s.status}</span>
            </td>
            <td>{s.act}</td>
            <td>{s.rules}</td>
            <td>{s.what}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Read that carefully, because it is counter-intuitive. What is in force today is entirely
    about building the regulator. Every duty that costs a business money lands together on
    13 May 2027.
  </p>

  <h2>Start with a rule</h2>
  <p>
    {rules.length} of 23 Rules published so far.
    <a href="/rules/">See the full index →</a>
  </p>

  <ul class="rule-list">
    {rules.slice(0, 8).map((r) => (
      <li>
        <span class="num">Rule {r.data.rule}</span>
        <span class="body">
          <a href={`/rules/${r.id}/`}>{r.data.title}</a>
          <span class="sub">{r.data.summary}</span>
        </span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</Base>
